---
// ACT 4c — the loop that learns, narrated as a design decision.
//
// The brief here isn't "show a feature," it's "show the THINKING." So the beat
// runs intent → feature → proof:
//   1 · INTENT  — my first-person reasoning: to learn fast, make the engine
//                 surface its single biggest confusion each round.
//   2 · FEATURE — the ask that produced: Richard names its most surprising
//                 finding, cites the real tally, and asks me one question.
//   3 · PROOF   — what that loop bought: the untouched ORIGINAL went from
//                 winning 67% of blind votes to 7% as the taste model sharpened.
import Richard from "./Richard.astro";
---

<section class="tl" data-tl>
  <!-- 1 · DESIGN INTENT (first person) -->
  <div class="tl-intent">
    <span class="tl-eyebrow tl-eyebrow-amber">the design problem, in my words</span>
    <p class="tl-intent-q">My goal was to build an engineer out of my own ear — one blind vote at a time. The question I kept circling: <b>how do I make that learning fast?</b></p>
    <p class="tl-intent-a">The move was to let the engine <b>ask</b>. If it surfaces its single most pressing point of confusion each round, every answer I give lands on the biggest gap — and a handful of targeted replies steer the whole trajectory faster than ten thousand silent votes ever could.</p>
    <span class="tl-intent-cue" aria-hidden="true">↓ so I built the part that asks</span>
  </div>

  <!-- 2 · THE FEATURE: the ask — mirrors Richard's actual box in the portal:
       his pond (green-water glow, teal rim, lily pads + reeds), the turtle
       speaking, his question in a teal speech bubble with a tail. -->
  <div class="tl-ask" data-tl-ask>
    <svg class="tl-pond" viewBox="0 0 400 58" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
      <g fill="none" stroke="#22d3ff" stroke-width="1.1" opacity="0.5" stroke-linecap="round">
        <path d="M0 30 q26 -7 52 0 t52 0 t52 0 t52 0 t52 0 t52 0 t52 0" />
        <path d="M0 42 q30 6 60 0 t60 0 t60 0 t60 0 t60 0 t60 0" opacity="0.7" />
      </g>
      <g opacity="0.9">
        <path d="M60 40 a17 7 0 1 0 34 0 a17 7 0 1 0 -34 0 M77 40 l9 -4" fill="#2f7a4c" stroke="#1f5a37" stroke-width="0.8" />
        <circle cx="76" cy="36" r="1.7" fill="#ffd23d" opacity="0.85" />
        <path d="M150 46 a13 5.5 0 1 0 26 0 a13 5.5 0 1 0 -26 0 M163 46 l7 -3" fill="#3f9e63" stroke="#27623f" stroke-width="0.8" />
        <path d="M300 41 a15 6 0 1 0 30 0 a15 6 0 1 0 -30 0 M315 41 l8 -3.5" fill="#2f7a4c" stroke="#1f5a37" stroke-width="0.8" />
        <circle cx="314" cy="37.5" r="1.6" fill="#ff7ab8" opacity="0.85" />
      </g>
      <g stroke="#4aa86a" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" fill="none">
        <path d="M356 56 q-3 -18 1 -30" /><path d="M366 56 q2 -16 -1 -28" /><path d="M376 56 q-2 -14 1 -24" />
      </g>
      <g fill="#9c6b3a"><rect x="355" y="22" width="3.6" height="9" rx="1.8" /><rect x="365" y="24" width="3.4" height="8" rx="1.7" /></g>
      <path d="M14 56 q4 -12 16 -11 q10 1 12 11 Z" fill="#525866" stroke="#3a3f4b" stroke-width="0.8" />
    </svg>

    <div class="tl-ask-head">
      <h4 class="tl-ask-name"><span aria-hidden="true">🐢</span> Richard</h4>
      <span class="tl-finding" data-tl-finding>surprise · original_dominates · “she can't hurt me”</span>
    </div>

    <div class="tl-speech">
      <div class="tl-avatar"><Richard size={88} speaking={true} /></div>
      <p class="tl-question" data-tl-q>You've crowned the <b>warmer</b> take on three tracks in a row now — and on
        <i>“she can't hurt me”</i> the original beat all six of my masters, 11 votes to 1. Should I
        assume you want vocals sitting <b>back</b> by default on songs like this — or keep slipping
        a bright take in to check myself?</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tl-answer" data-tl-answerwrap>
      <textarea class="tl-input" data-tl-input placeholder="Tell Richard (⌘↵ to send)…">Lean warm by default, but always keep one bright take so I don't drift.</textarea>
      <div class="tl-answer-row">
        <button type="button" class="tl-skip" data-tl-skip>skip</button>
        <button type="button" class="tl-send" data-tl-send>Send ⌘↵</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="tl-result" data-tl-result aria-live="polite"></p>
  </div>

  <!-- 3 · THE PROOF -->
  <div class="tl-learn">
    <span class="tl-eyebrow tl-eyebrow-green">what the loop bought</span>
    <div class="tl-stat" data-tl-stat>
      <div class="tl-stat-row">
        <span class="tl-stat-label">the untouched <b>ORIGINAL</b> beat every master…</span>
        <span class="tl-stat-bars">
          <span class="tl-stat-from"><b data-tl-from>67</b>%</span>
          <span class="tl-stat-arrow">→</span>
          <span class="tl-stat-to"><b data-tl-to>7</b>%</span>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="tl-bar-track"><span class="tl-bar-fill" data-tl-bar></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="tl-copy">
      Early on, mastering by splitting stems left artifacts no processing could remove — so the
      untouched take kept winning. Switching to full-track mastering, then letting every blind vote
      and every answer above re-weight which records it reaches for, flipped that almost completely.
      Three axis winners per song, and it <b>synthesizes a king</b> from what they share.
    </p>
    <div class="tl-lean" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="tl-lean-label">learned lean</span>
      <span class="tl-chip tl-chip-on">warm</span>
      <span class="tl-chip tl-chip-on">punchy</span>
      <span class="tl-chip tl-chip-on">dynamic</span>
      <span class="tl-chip">brittle highs</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-tl]").forEach((root) => {
    const reduce = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
    const fromEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-tl-from]");
    const toEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-tl-to]");
    const bar = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-tl-bar]");
    const input = root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-tl-input]");
    const sendBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-tl-send]");
    const skipBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-tl-skip]");
    const result = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-tl-result]");
    const answerWrap = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-tl-answerwrap]");
    const bubbleQ = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-tl-q]");

    // animate the 67 → 7 drop when the stat scrolls in
    let ran = false;
    const animate = () => {
      if (ran) return; ran = true;
      if (bar) bar.style.width = "7%";
      if (reduce) { if (fromEl) fromEl.textContent = "67"; if (toEl) toEl.textContent = "7"; return; }
      const start = performance.now();
      const tick = (now: number) => {
        const t = Math.min(1, (now - start) / 1100);
        const eased = 1 - Math.pow(1 - t, 3);
        if (toEl) toEl.textContent = String(Math.round(67 - 60 * eased));
        if (t < 1) requestAnimationFrame(tick);
      };
      requestAnimationFrame(tick);
      window.setTimeout(() => { if (toEl) toEl.textContent = "7"; }, 1250);
    };
    const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      for (const e of entries) if (e.isIntersecting) { animate(); io.disconnect(); }
    }, { threshold: 0.5 });
    const statEl = root.querySelector("[data-tl-stat]");
    if (statEl) io.observe(statEl);

    const send = () => {
      const note = input?.value.trim() || "";
      if (answerWrap) answerWrap.style.display = "none";
      if (bubbleQ) bubbleQ.innerHTML = "Got it. I'll lean <b>warm</b> on tracks that sound like this one, and keep one bright take in every batch to check myself.";
      if (result) result.innerHTML = `✓ folded into your taste — <b>bounded ±0.30, scoped to tracks like this</b>. It tunes which references I pick, not the win-rate model.`;
    };
    sendBtn?.addEventListener("click", send);
    input?.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => { if ((e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && e.key === "Enter") send(); });
    skipBtn?.addEventListener("click", () => {
      if (answerWrap) answerWrap.style.display = "none";
      if (result) result.textContent = "skipped — I'll ask again once I've seen a few more of your crowns.";
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .tl {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 22px;
    color: #f5f1e8; max-width: 760px;
  }

  .tl-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .tl-eyebrow-amber { color: var(--brand-yellow); }
  .tl-eyebrow-cyan { color: var(--brand-cyan); margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .tl-eyebrow-green { color: var(--brand-green); }

  /* ── 1 · intent (designer's voice) ── */
  .tl-intent { border-left: 2px solid var(--brand-yellow); padding-left: 18px; }
  .tl-intent-q, .tl-intent-a {
    margin: 0 0 12px; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.62; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.82);
  }
  .tl-intent-q { font-size: 16px; color: #f5f1e8; }
  .tl-intent-q b { color: var(--brand-yellow); }
  .tl-intent-a b { color: #f5f1e8; }
  .tl-intent-cue {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--brand-cyan); font-style: italic;
  }

  /* ── 2 · the ask — Richard's pond box, mirroring his portal surface:
        a green-water glow from the base, a teal-cyan rim, the pond scene along
        the bottom, the turtle speaking into a teal bubble with a tail. ── */
  .tl-ask {
    position: relative; overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 18px; padding: 18px 22px 20px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(135% 90% at 50% 122%, rgba(34, 168, 99, 0.13), transparent 62%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(15, 21, 25, 0.96), rgba(9, 13, 15, 0.975));
    border: 1px solid rgba(34, 211, 255, 0.24);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 44px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.42), 0 0 60px rgba(34, 168, 99, 0.07);
  }
  .tl-pond { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; width: 100%; height: 58px; z-index: 0; opacity: 0.5; pointer-events: none; }
  .tl-ask > .tl-ask-head, .tl-ask > .tl-speech, .tl-ask > .tl-answer, .tl-ask > .tl-result { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .tl-ask-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .tl-ask-name { margin: 0; font-family: "Space Grotesk Variable", "Space Grotesk", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 17px; color: #f4eee3; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .tl-finding { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.5); }
  .tl-speech { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 16px; margin: 14px 0 18px; }
  .tl-avatar { flex: 0 0 auto; margin-top: 2px; filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 12px rgba(34, 211, 255, 0.22)); }
  .tl-question {
    position: relative; flex: 1 1 auto; margin: 0; padding: 14px 18px;
    font-family: "Geist Variable", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: #f4eee3; text-wrap: pretty;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(34, 211, 255, 0.11), rgba(34, 168, 99, 0.05));
    border: 1px solid rgba(34, 211, 255, 0.3);
    border-radius: 6px 16px 16px 16px;
    box-shadow: 0 0 24px rgba(34, 211, 255, 0.1), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  }
  .tl-question::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: -7px; top: 18px; width: 13px; height: 13px;
    background: rgba(34, 211, 255, 0.11);
    border-left: 1px solid rgba(34, 211, 255, 0.3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(34, 211, 255, 0.3);
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }
  .tl-question b { color: var(--brand-cyan); font-weight: 600; }
  .tl-question i { color: #fff; font-style: italic; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .tl-speech { gap: 10px; } }
  .tl-input {
    width: 100%; background: rgba(7, 6, 12, 0.6); border: 1px solid rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.18);
    border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px 12px; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 12.5px; color: #f5f1e8; line-height: 1.45; resize: vertical; min-height: 58px; outline: none;
    transition: border-color 160ms ease;
  }
  .tl-input:focus { border-color: rgba(14, 196, 252, 0.5); }
  .tl-answer-row { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; gap: 8px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .tl-skip, .tl-send {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 12px; cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: 5px; padding: 7px 14px; transition: filter 160ms ease, color 160ms ease, border-color 160ms ease;
  }
  .tl-skip { background: transparent; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.2); color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.55); }
  .tl-skip:hover { color: #f5f1e8; border-color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.4); }
  .tl-send { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #0ec4fc, #19e0ff); border: none; color: #062330; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; }
  .tl-send:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }
  .tl-result { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--brand-cyan); margin: 12px 0 0; }
  .tl-result b { color: #f5f1e8; }

  /* ── 3 · the proof ── */
  .tl-stat {
    background: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.02); border: 1px solid rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.1);
    border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 18px; margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .tl-stat-row { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .tl-stat-label { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 12px; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.6); }
  .tl-stat-label b { color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.85); font-weight: 700; }
  .tl-stat-bars { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-feature-settings: "tnum"; }
  .tl-stat-from { font-size: 16px; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.5); }
  .tl-stat-from b { font-style: italic; font-weight: 700; }
  .tl-stat-arrow { color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.4); }
  .tl-stat-to { font-size: 28px; color: var(--brand-green); }
  .tl-stat-to b { font-style: italic; font-weight: 700; }
  .tl-bar-track { height: 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: rgba(255, 39, 97, 0.18); overflow: hidden; }
  .tl-bar-fill { display: block; height: 100%; width: 67%; border-radius: 4px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--brand-green), #7dffa6); transition: width 1100ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1); }

  .tl-copy { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.66); margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .tl-copy b { color: #f5f1e8; }
  .tl-lean { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .tl-lean-label { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.4); margin-right: 4px; }
  .tl-chip {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 11px; padding: 4px 11px; border-radius: 20px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.16); color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.5);
  }
  .tl-chip-on { color: #0d060f; border-color: transparent; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff2d8b, #ff7a3d, #ffd23d); font-weight: 700; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .tl-bar-fill { transition: none; } }
</style>
